  "priorExpiration": "1997-04-04",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Den 101.13 “Direct supervision” means a dentist with an active license is in the dental office, authorizes the procedure and remains in the dental office while the procedures are being performed and evaluates the performance of the dental hygienist or dental assistant before dismissal of the patient.\n\nSource. #287.2 eff 1-17-74; ss by #2981, eff 2-28-85; ss by #5110, eff 4-4-91, EXPIRED: 4-4-97\n\nNew. #6908, eff 12-9-98; ss by #10990, eff 12-9-15; renumbered by #12427 (formerly Den 101.10); renumbered by #14140 (formerly Den 101.11)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/den100-500.html"
